      "provenance": {
        "notes": "NAME CLASH: 'geranium' is Pelargonium; the hardy cranesbill Geranium is a different plant. Separate row from the zonal pelargonium (row 53): trailing habit, baskets. Watering: RHS profile says moderate in spring and summer, sparingly in winter, letting compost dry between waterings; the NC State genus page agrees for containers; mapped to let_top_dry (agent). Light: the RHS growing guide says most pelargoniums flower best in full sun; the profile says full sun or partial shade. Size: RHS 0.1 to 0.5 m both ways (trails further in baskets). Growth rate and toxicity come from the NC State genus page (medium; low severity, geraniol and linalool, leaves, vomiting, cats most sensitive), not a page about this species, so both are the agent's reading. The RHS profile is silent on toxicity. No page gives tolerances, rest factor, humidity or an indoor temperature."
      },
